### Architecture Notes
- src/owlbear/config.py already contains env_nested_delimiter='__' and a browser field, so #553 is now a finish-the-integration task rather than a from-scratch implementation.
- The remaining architectural gap is the leaf-node violation: src/owlbear/config.py imports BrowserConfig from src/owlbear/tools/browser/config.py. Moving the class into config.py removes the forbidden config -> tools edge and stops import owlbear.config from preloading the parent owlbear.tools package through that path.
- The four remaining BrowserConfig() constructions are in src/owlbear/bootstrap/hooks.py, src/owlbear/bootstrap/toolsets.py, src/owlbear/bootstrap/knowledge.py, and src/owlbear/bootstrap/__init__.py. _build_web_search_toolset and _build_hydrator will need signature updates to receive settings.
- src/owlbear/tools/browser/manager.py and src/owlbear/tools/browser/toolset.py should keep their current local fallbacks (config or BrowserConfig()). That preserves direct-construction behavior outside bootstrap.
- Do not widen scope into src/owlbear/tools/__init__.py. Any broader package side-effect cleanup stays with #857 and #859.

### Changes Made
- Verified the current src/ and tests/ state instead of relying on the older research doc alone.
- Verified #843 exists, is archived, and already covers the RED-phase nested-env regression cases in tests/test_config.py.
- Approved #553 to todo without rewriting the implementation contract; the existing implementation-facing AC lines remain mechanically verifiable.

### Dependencies
- Verified: #843 archived and dependency satisfied.
- Verified impacted modules: src/owlbear/config.py, src/owlbear/bootstrap/hooks.py, src/owlbear/bootstrap/toolsets.py, src/owlbear/bootstrap/knowledge.py, src/owlbear/bootstrap/__init__.py, src/owlbear/tools/browser/config.py.